        <item>
            <title>3.24.0</title>
            <pubDate>Wed, 11 Nov 2026 14:49:57 +0900</pubDate>
            <link>https://github.com/Saqoosha/Canopy</link>
            <sparkle:version>221</sparkle:version>
            <sparkle:shortVersionString>3.24.0</sparkle:shortVersionString>
            <sparkle:minimumSystemVersion>15.0</sparkle:minimumSystemVersion>
            <sparkle:hardwareRequirements>arm64</sparkle:hardwareRequirements>
            <description sparkle:format="markdown"><![CDATA[### Changes
- Moving a session to another folder no longer asks for confirmation every time. Canopy now asks only when Claude Code config (a `.claude` folder or `.mcp.json`) in that folder could have come from outside your Mac: committed to git in the repository or any of its worktrees, present anywhere in a non-git folder, or a `.mcp.json` in a folder above. When it does ask, the dialog lists the hooks, MCP servers and permissions it found.
- Repositories from GitHub owners you trust can skip the check: `defaults write sh.saqoo.Canopy canopy.trustedRemoteOwners -array <owner>`. A fork's pull request checked out locally is still checked.

### Bug Fixes
- Continuing a folder's latest session from the launcher now sends the typed prompt and the chosen model, effort, permission and provider. Before, they were dropped.
]]></description>
